# Agent contract

`AGENTS.md` at the repository root is binding. Read it in full before any
other work and follow it; it overrides every other rule file here.

- Workflow: research with the Graphify knowledge graph, plan, failing test
  first, implement, review, verify.
- Before finishing or committing run `go run ./tools/eccgate verify`; it must
  print `RESULT: READY`.
- Never use `--no-verify`, never change `core.hooksPath`, never edit the gate
  (`.golangci.yml`, `.githooks/`, `tools/eccgate/`, CI workflows) to make it pass.
- Code must be industrial-grade: read `.claude/rules/project/industrial-standards.md`
  (`AGENTS.md` section 9) before writing Go.
- On a hard problem, stop and research before planning: follow
  `.claude/rules/project/research-first.md` (`AGENTS.md` section 10), record the
  result under `docs/research/`, and list every new direct dependency in
  `docs/research/dependencies.md`.
- Role playbooks are in `.claude/agents/`, skills in `.claude/skills/`.
